From 585ad2a4547cd3c9f01361b706b217eb4bcb1eab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:26:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: the dual-texture post transform, so lava has its
 colour

GX can send a texgen's result through a second matrix from post-transform
memory (XF 0x500-0x5FF, chosen per texgen by XF 0x1050-0x1057, on since
GXInit writes XF 0x1012 = 1). The renderer never read either, so a texgen
used its texture matrix alone. Wind Waker's lava (d_magma.cpp) is the one
user: its crust pattern and its colour ramp (the ramp indexed by height) are
both projected through post matrices, and without them the lava in Dragon
Roost Cavern and Gohma's room drew white (orange-brown blotches on the Mac).

The front end keeps post-transform memory beside DolGxRecompState (so the
saved front-end state keeps its size and 0.3.0 save states still load), and
each draw carries the rows of any regular texgen whose post matrix is not
the identity. gxcore folds them into that texgen's matrix rows, post * tex,
as Dolphin's VertexShaderGen applies them; no shader or pipeline key
changes, so shader caches stay valid. A post transform that normalizes
first is not folded (nothing in Wind Waker uses one).

Checked: gxcore_tests (with a fold test for three- and two-row texgens);
Gohma's room draws orange lava with its dark crust, real and in-between
frames; Outset's synchronous captures 19 of 19 and Smooth Motion dumps
62 of 62 identical to the release's.
